  "live_records": {
    "q-277800": {
      "dom_id": "step-q277800",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "From **left to right,** the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}=144$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand \n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =144 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-16(0)^{2} & =144 \\\\ 9{x}^{2} & =144 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $(-4,0)$ and $(4,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
