    "q-278363": {
      "dom_id": "step-q278363",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $6{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2}=30$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =30 \\\\ 6{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =30 \\\\ 6{y}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,-\\sqrt{5}).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
