    "q-8011": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8011",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Calculate the points where the hyperbola \n$25{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=26$\nintersects the line $x=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=1,$ we substitute $x=1$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =26 \\\\ 25(1)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =26 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =26-25 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. \nSo, the hyperbola does not intersect the vertical line $x=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
