    "q-278371": {
      "dom_id": "step-q278371",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "The hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1$ intersects the line $x=-3$ at\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-3,$ we substitute $x=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $x=-3$ at $(-3,0).$",
