    "q-278384": {
      "dom_id": "step-q278384",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "From **left to right**, the points where the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=16$ intersects the line $y=2.5$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=2.5,$ we substitute $y=2.5$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4(2.5)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 25-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & =16-25 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & =-9 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $y=2.5$  at the points $(-3,2.5)$ and $(3,2.5).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
