    "q-10489": {
      "dom_id": "step-q10489",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y=-x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-x)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
