    "q-8010": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8010",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-{y}^{2}=1$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x,$ we first replace $y$ with $\\frac{1}{3}x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 0 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the last equation is a false statement, we conclude that the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
