    "q-8002": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8002",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $5{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=16$ intersects the line $y=x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
