    "q-278379": {
      "dom_id": "step-q278379",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=20$ intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x,$ we first replace $y$ with $\\sqrt{5}x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-\\sqrt{5}$ and $x=\\sqrt{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
