    "q-278374": {
      "dom_id": "step-q278374",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{12{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
